THIRD-PARTY DATA
================

FlahaX ships numerical data from the sources below. Each value keeps its
citation in the data file named. Numerical facts are cited, not relicensed:
the Apache-2.0 license covers FlahaX's code and its own compilation, not the
underlying measurements.

1. USGS PHREEQC 3.8.6 thermodynamic data (src/flahax/data/chemistry_25c.json)
   - 205 aqueous species, phases and equilibrium constants at 25 C from the
     database minteq.v4.dat, distributed with PHREEQC by the U.S. Geological
     Survey (source pinned by SHA-256
     ab0a8f7c7375e1bd997990f4bc3a9af497516f10e57f4aaa3cefb55dccac5ae7,
     https://github.com/usgs-coupled-subtrees/phreeqc3-database/blob/master/minteq.v4.dat).
     minteq.v4.dat derives from the U.S. EPA MINTEQA2 version 4 database.
   - Phase constants for kieserite (log K -0.123) and sylvite (log K 0.9)
     from the PHREEQC 3.8.6 database pitzer.dat.
   - MODIFICATIONS: these records are not the original files. Rafat A. Al
     Khashan converted the 25 C constants to JSON for FlahaX (first
     committed 2026-09-27), keeping only the species and phases FlahaX
     uses, and added FlahaX extensions marked in the file by their own
     "source" field (flahax-chelates-25c.dat, flahax-phases-25c.dat). The
     original database is available from the USGS at the URL above.
   - The USGS User Rights Notice for PHREEQC applies to this data and is
     reproduced in full at the end of this file.
   - Please acknowledge: Parkhurst, D. L. and Appelo, C. A. J. (2013)
     Description of input and examples for PHREEQC version 3, U.S.
     Geological Survey Techniques and Methods 6-A43, doi:10.3133/tm6A43;
     and the USGS.

2. FlahaX thermodynamic extensions (chemistry_25c.json, source fields
   flahax-chelates-25c.dat and flahax-phases-25c.dat)
   - Struvite: Ronteltap, Maurer and Gujer (2007), Water Research 41,
     977-984, doi:10.1016/j.watres.2006.11.046.
   - o,o-EDDHA: Yunta et al. (2003), Inorganic Chemistry 42, 5412-5421,
     doi:10.1021/ic034333j.
   - DTPA: Smith and Martell critical stability constants and NIST SRD 46.
   Details: docs/site/models/flahax-chelate-thermodynamic-profile.md.

3. Electrical conductivity (src/flahax/data/conductivity_mccleskey2012.json)
   - McCleskey, Nordstrom, Ryan and Ball (2012), Geochimica et
     Cosmochimica Acta 77, 369-382, doi:10.1016/j.gca.2011.10.031, Table 1.
   - Pethybridge, Talbot and House (2006), Journal of Solution Chemistry
     35, 381-393, doi:10.1007/s10953-005-9003-z, Table IV.
   - CRC Handbook of Chemistry and Physics, 85th ed., Vanysek, Ionic
     conductivity and diffusion at infinite dilution; PHREEQC phreeqc.dat
     diffusion coefficients.
   - Manufacturer EC anchors (src/flahax/calculated_ec.py): SQM, Ultrasol
     Macronutrients brochure, page 2.

4. Stock solubility (src/flahax/data/solubility.json, owner-approved
   2026-10-23)
   - CRC Handbook of Chemistry and Physics (ed. D. R. Lide), Aqueous
     Solubility of Inorganic Compounds at Various Temperatures,
     pp. 8-112 to 8-117 (18 products).
   - Yara, YaraTera CALCINIT product sheet (calcium nitrate, ag grade).
   - U.S. Coast Guard CHRIS / NOAA CAMEO Chemicals, Urea (URE), item 9.24.

5. Fertilizer catalogue and identities (src/flahax/data/library.json,
   material_identities.json)
   - Product assays from supplier documents named in each record: Haifa
     Group (Haifa Cal NG technical data sheet), Sigma-Aldrich (ACS reagent
     specifications), ChemicalBook technical data sheets.
   - Owner-supplied product analyses and properties: Flaha Agri Tech,
     Flaha Agri Tech Analysis Ver 0.0 (2026-10-29), an owner-declared
     catalogue review, not independent laboratory or lot verification.
   - Chemical identities and theoretical analyses: FlahaX materials audit,
     docs/audit/2026-10-18-materials-identity.

6. Concentrate-tank compatibility (src/flahax/tank_grouping.py)
   - Yara, Fertilizantes para fertirrigacion, p. 65 mixing compatibility
     table and p. 63 mixing rules.

7. Crop formulas (src/flahax/data/library.json, "formulas")
   - Published nutrient formulas as named in the library: Howard Resh;
     Douglas Peckenpaugh; maximumyield; Growing Edge; schundler.com; and the Hoagland solution (Hoagland and Arnon).

